rison and its vicinity], dated in the parade 'January 25th 1808', with its 'Index annexed to the Draught of Fort Dearborn &c.' signed at Fort Dearborn 20 February 1808. Original in the files of the War Department, Washington. Reproduced as the plate 'Fort Dearborn and Vicinity in 1808. From the original draft by Captain Whistler in the archives of the War Department at Washington', facing p. 164 of Quaife, Chicago and the Old Northwest, 1673-1835 (Chicago, 1913); the index is printed in full in note 413 on the same pages.","source_id":"whistler_1808_fort_dearborn_draught","tier":1,"tier_label":"period/eyewitness","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/69274/69274-h/images/fpage164_lg.png","what_it_does_not_supply":["any building height: the folded elevations disagree with each other","the fort's bearing to true north: no north arrow was found on the reproduction","the covered way to the river and the gutters, which the index itself says are omitted","anything about the second fort of 1816"],"what_it_supplies":["the first fort's garrison in plan at a stated scale: the double row of pickets, the two blockhouses at the north-west and south-east angles, the four barracks ranges, the magazine, two small houses, the main gate, the parade and the flagstaff","the drafter's index of 34 numbered features, and the note that two of them (the covered way and the gutters) are omitted from their places","the arrangement of the factor's and agent's establishments, stables, gardens and the houses across the river, by position only and not to scale"]},"uses":["other_scene","research"]}
